## #02 — Compose the accepted reader; do not recreate it
For explicitly requested members on disposable member copies, invoke the pinned
reader inspect --book ABS --member NAME --json. Store exact returned bytes, exit,
observation time and source kind under the attempt as live inspection evidence,
separate from commit-blob references. Reuse its schema/status/reservation/capture
projection, including origin, submission and receipt/manifest identities when
complete. No parsing human verify prose or parallel receipt/package validator.
Reject malformed tool JSON/unknown schema or inconsistent status/exit as an explicit
failed observation. Hash-check inspector and required sibling before invoking.
No helper/parser/core changes. A tool mismatch never launches that dependency.

## #03 — Readiness, material and stability
An empty member list remains valid. A requested member is required evidence for
THIS fixture slice: missing/reserved/incomplete/refused or unavailable structured
identity must be explicit remediation and cannot yield oriented. Do not manufacture
capture identities for those states. Receipt completeness proves custody only;
review/acceptance/publication may exist elsewhere and cannot be inferred absent.
Make included member evidence actually readable/citable in the model's bounded
packet. Count its raw material/ref footprint against the existing12-ref/128KiB
limits; preserve full sources in attempt records, with explicit omissions and
partial readiness on overflow. Keep committed Git text distinct. Observation refs
do not silently expand the set of eligible work targets for O1.
Reobserve required member identities at prepare end; changed state/receipt identity
marks the attempt unstable/partial, not a coherent ready packet. Record the actual
observations; do not claim an atomic filesystem snapshot or protection against a
same-user swap between reads. No changes to old attempts or semantic grading.

